---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const webManifest = `{
  "manifest_version": 1,
  "id": "dev.example.worklog",
  "name": "Worklog",
  "homepage": "https://worklog.example",
  "icon": "https://worklog.example/icon.png",
  "redirect_uris": [
    "https://worklog.example/auth/mdbase/callback",
    "dev.example.worklog://auth/mdbase/callback"
  ],
  "requirements": {
    "access": "full_collection",
    "contracts": [
      {
        "id": "example.work-item",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "digest": "sha256:9cd7f8e4b23ba20aaeaec3f7e209c6ba8de3fa5cd224204f2baef4e14dd69936"
      }
    ],
    "capabilities": {
      "contract_version": 2,
      "required": ["collection.read", "records.create", "records.edit"],
      "optional": ["records.delete"]
    }
  }
}`;

const provision = `"provisions": {
  "type_packs": [
    {
      "provides": [
        {
          "id": "example.work-item",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "digest": "sha256:9cd7f8e4…"
        }
      ],
      "manifest": {
        "kind": "mdbase.type-pack",
        "id": "example.work-items",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "name": "Work items",
        "resources": [
          {
            "kind": "contract",
            "source": "contracts/example.work-item.md",
            "target": "_contracts/example.work-item.md",
            "digest": "sha256:9cd7f8e4…"
          },
          {
            "kind": "type",
            "source": "types/work-item.md",
            "target": "_types/work-item.md",
            "digest": "sha256:2be7d8a5…"
          }
        ]
      },
      "resources": [
        { "source": "contracts/example.work-item.md", "document": "---\\nkind: mdbase.contract\\n…" },
        { "source": "types/work-item.md", "document": "---\\nkind: mdbase.type\\n…" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Application manifest"
  description="One JSON file says who your app is, which collections suit it, and what it may do."
  active="manifest"
  headings={[
    { href: "#identity", label: "Identity" },
    { href: "#web", label: "Web apps" },
    { href: "#requirements", label: "Requirements" },
    { href: "#provisioning", label: "Provisioning" },
    { href: "#portable", label: "Notifications" },
    { href: "#native", label: "Native apps" },
    { href: "#changes", label: "Changing it" }
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Ship the manifest with your app and pass it to
    {" "}<code>MdbaseConnect</code>. The SDK validates it with the same parser
    mdbase uses. Schema:
    {" "}<a href="/connect/schemas/mdbase-app.v1.json"><code>mdbase-app.v1.json</code></a>.
    The whole file may be at most 512 KiB.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={webManifest} language="json" label="mdbase-app.json" />

  <h2 id="identity">Identity</h2>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Field</th>
        <th>Rule</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>manifest_version</code></td><td><code>1</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>Lowercase reverse-domain name with at least three parts, such as <code>dev.example.worklog</code>. It is a label, not proof of who publishes the app.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>Shown to the user when they approve your app; up to 100 characters</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>icon</code></td><td>Optional HTTPS URL</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="web">Web apps</h2>
  <p>
    A web app declares an HTTPS <code>homepage</code> and up to ten
    {" "}<code>redirect_uris</code> on the homepage’s origin.
    {" "}<code>distribution</code> may be left out; it defaults to
    {" "}<code>"web"</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Field</th>
        <th>Meaning</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>access</code></td>
        <td>Required. Always <code>"full_collection"</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>contracts</code></td>
        <td>
          Required, may be empty. Each entry names a contract by
          {" "}<code>id</code>, <code>version</code> and exact
          {" "}<code>digest</code>. A collection suits your app when its types
          implement them. See <a href="/sdk/contracts/">Contracts and adapters</a>.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>capabilities</code></td>
        <td>
          What your app may do. See <a href="/sdk/authorization/">Authorization</a>.
          Without it, your app gets read-only access.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>files</code></td>
        <td>File actions and the folders they apply to</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>people</code></td>
        <td>
          <code>identity</code> (who the user is) and <code>members</code>
          {" "}(the collection’s members), as <code>required</code> or
          {" "}<code>optional</code>, with <code>"version": 1</code>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>configuration</code></td>
        <td>
          Values the collection’s settings must contain, each with an
          {" "}<code>id</code>, a <code>path</code>, the predicate
          {" "}<code>"contains"</code> and a <code>value</code>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="provisioning">Provisioning</h2>
  <p>
    If a collection lacks the contract you need, your manifest can carry a
    type pack that adds it. Every resource is pinned by digest. The pack is
    checked as a whole and written all at once or not at all. A pack may only
    provide contracts listed in <code>requirements.contracts</code>. A target
    file that already exists with different bytes is a conflict, never
    overwritten.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={provision} language="json" label="Manifest fragment (digests shortened)" />
  <p>
    <code>provisions.configuration</code> can likewise add a value to the
    collection’s settings, with the operation <code>"set_add"</code>, to meet a
    {" "}<code>configuration</code> requirement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="portable">Notifications</h2>
  <p>
    <code>notifications.criteria</code> declares the notifications your app
    may send, with fixed titles and text. See
    {" "}<a href="/sdk/notifications/">Notifications and timers</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="native">Native apps</h2>
  <p>
    A native app can list a private-use URI scheme in
    {" "}<code>redirect_uris</code>. The scheme must match or extend the
    application ID, as in <code>dev.example.worklog://auth/mdbase/callback</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changing the manifest</h2>
  <p>
    A changed manifest never widens an existing grant on its own. If your new
    version needs more, such as a new capability or contract, the user
    approves it again.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
